Code Function and Results (40/50 Points)
	
	The instructions stated to use a range of buffer sizes in powers of 2 from 1 to 12. 

	I understand that it could be read more ambiguously, such as selecting some buffer sizes
	from within that range. But you should at least use the same buffer sizes in the tests 
	for UDP and TCP in order to make a comparison.  

	Your TCP implementation is also a bit unique in that you sent an ack every message. This
	is no doubt responsible for the extreme time it took to complete. I imagine it influenced 
	your decision to use less buffer sizes in the smaller range.

	Your UDP implementation however, follows a better pattern where an ack is sent only once 
	after the total message is sent. This makes the two very hard to compare. 

	For these reasons I will deduct just a partial amount of points concerning the variety of buffer sizes. However 
	I also have to consider the inconsistency between TCP and UDP implementations and the effect on measurement.
	

